ttychatter.mailbot walkthrough
==============================

1. Install the program
----------------------

    mkdir -p /home/r94/bin
    cp ttychatter.mailbot /home/r94/bin/
    chmod 700 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot

2. Confirm the bot can run
--------------------------

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --version
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --help

3. Configure IMAP and sending
-----------------------------

Example config:

    IMAP_HOST=localhost
    IMAP_PORT=993
    IMAP_SSL=1
    IMAP_USER=r94
    IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE=/home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg

    MAIL_FROM=ttychatter@thatiam.vip
    ALLOWED_FROM=r94@thatiam.vip

    REPLY_METHOD=sendmail
    SENDMAIL=/usr/sbin/sendmail

    TTYCHATTER_COMMAND=/home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python
    SESSION_DIR=/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
    ATTACHMENT_DIR=/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments

    SUBJECT_PREFIX=tc
    MAX_BODY_BYTES=50000
    PROCESS_ATTACHMENTS=1

4. Store the IMAP password
--------------------------

    export GPG_TTY=$(tty)
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --set-imap-password --gpg

5. Check diagnostics
--------------------

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --config
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --doctor

6. Candidate debugging
----------------------

If a message is unread but not processed:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates

This prints each unread candidate, its sender, its subject, and why it matches
or is skipped. It uses BODY.PEEK[] and does not mark messages read.

7. Dry-run a normal mail request
--------------------------------

Send yourself an unread mail with subject:

    tc:{mailbot-test}

Then run:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run

Dry-run must not mark the email read.

8. Real one-shot run
--------------------

After dry-run looks correct:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once

9. Config by email
------------------

To request the config:

    Subject: tc:{CONFIG}

The bot replies with ttychatter-mailbot-config.txt attached. Edit that file and
reply with it attached under the same subject. The bot will backup the old config
and replace it with the attached config.

Dry-run is safe:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run

It will not write config and will not mark the config mail read.

10. Cron
--------

Once everything works:

    */2 * * * * /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once >>/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/mailbot.log 2>&1
